"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[7871],{78238:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"getPlayerRootPosition","desc":"Position of the local character\'s PrimaryPart, or nil when there is no\\ncharacter. Used as the default spawn origin.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":422,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"spawnDrop","desc":"Spawns one drop and starts its arc. Returns the resolved [Drop], or nil if\\nno origin could be determined (no `data.origin` and no character).\\n\\n`data.particle` accepts either an Instance to clone or an image asset id;\\na string builds an invisible part carrying a 24x24 `BillboardGui` with\\nthat image, so UI-style drops and 3D-model drops share one code path.\\n\\n```lua\\nDropsController.spawnDrop({\\n\\tparticle = ReplicatedStorage.Assets.Resources.Stone:Clone(),\\n\\torigin = hitPosition + Vector3.new(0, 2, 0),\\n\\ttweenToCharacterOnClaim = true,\\n\\tautoClaimOnDestruction = true,\\n\\tonClaim = function()\\n\\t\\tDropsController.showChange(1, \\"item\\", \\"Stone\\")\\n\\tend,\\n})\\n```\\n\\n:::caution\\nWhen `data.onClaim` is set the particle is *not* added to the maid\\ndirectly \u2014 the maid\'s cleanup function fires `onClaim` and then destroys\\nthe part, unless a pickup lerp still owns it. That is why claimed parts\\nare tracked separately in `claimedParts`.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"data","desc":"Drop description","lua_type":"DropData"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Drop?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":462,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"updateDrops","desc":"Expiry sweep. Driven every RenderStepped by the connection\\n[DropsController.init] opens; safe to call by hand.\\n\\nRetires every drop older than its `lifetime`, skipping any already\\n`destroying`. Drops flagged `autoClaimOnDestruction` go through\\n[DropsController.pickupDrop] with `forcePickup` so their `onClaim` still\\nruns; the rest are dropped with [DropsController.removeDrop].","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":641,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"removeDrop","desc":"Retires one drop without claiming it: marks it `destroying`, destroys the\\nparticle (with a `CoinDespawn` burst when `SHOW_DESPAWN_VFX` is on),\\ndestroys the maid, and clears it from `activeDrops` and `claimedParts`.\\n\\nNote the maid\'s own cleanup still fires `onClaim` if the drop had one \u2014\\nso a caller relying on `onClaim` for the reward is not silently skipped\\nwhen the drop is removed rather than picked up. Unknown ids are ignored.","params":[{"name":"dropId","desc":"Key into the active-drops table","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":675,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"clearAllDrops","desc":"Destroys every active drop\'s maid and resets the registry and the id\\ncounter. Used by [DropsController.shutdown] and by anything that needs a\\nclean slate, such as a teleport or round transition.\\n\\nUnlike [DropsController.removeDrop] this does not destroy particles\\ndirectly \u2014 it relies on each maid\'s cleanup, which means `onClaim`\\ncallbacks still fire.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":714,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"showChange","desc":"Floating \\"+N\\" popup welded to the local character. Independent of the drop\\nsystem \u2014 call it whenever a currency or item total moves.\\n\\nCalls coalesce. The first call clones `Assets.UI.GainVFX`, welds it to the\\nPrimaryPart and tweens its `StudsOffset` upward over `PARTICLE_TEXT_LIFE`\\nseconds. Subsequent calls within that window add to the running total and\\npush the expiry out instead of spawning a second billboard, so a burst of\\nten single-coin awards reads as one \\"+10\\".\\n\\nEach distinct `{unitType}_{itemId}` gets its own label row cloned from the\\nbillboard\'s `Template`, so mixed gains stack:\\n\\n```lua\\nDropsController.showChange(1, \\"coins\\")\\nDropsController.showChange(1, \\"item\\", \\"Tree\\")\\n```\\n\\nIcons resolve from `Items[itemId].icon` for items and `CoreImages[\\"styled/coin\\"]`\\nfor coins; a row with no icon falls back to showing the identifier as text\\nand destroys its icon label. No-ops when the character has no PrimaryPart.","params":[{"name":"amount","desc":"Added to the running total for this unit","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"unitType","desc":"Which family of gain","lua_type":"\\"coins\\" | \\"item\\""},{"name":"itemId","desc":"Item to resolve an icon for, when `unitType` is \\"item\\"","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":778,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"init","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Resets the registry and opens the RenderStepped connection\\nthat drives [DropsController.updateDrops].\\n\\nPaired with [DropsController.start], which opens the claim loop. Both are\\ncalled by `Bootstrap` during `Entry.client.luau` step 4.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":938,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"pickupDrop","desc":"Claims one drop, if it is claimable. Called for every active drop each\\nframe by [DropsController.checkClaims], and directly with\\n`forcePickup = true` by [DropsController.updateDrops] for drops flagged\\n`autoClaimOnDestruction`.\\n\\nUnless `forcePickup` is set, the drop is skipped when any of these hold:\\n\\n* it is flagged `destroyOnArrival` (it was already retired on landing)\\n* the character is further than `DEFAULT_CLAIM_RADIUS` studs from\\n  `targetPosition`\\n* less than `CLAIM_DELAY` seconds have passed since spawn\\n* it is already `claimed`, or currently `destroying`\\n\\nWith `tweenToCharacterOnClaim`, the spawn maid is destroyed outright to\\nstop the float, the trail is re-enabled, and a fresh RenderStepped\\nconnection lerps the part toward the character\'s pivot \u2014 re-read every\\nframe \u2014 over `CHARACTER_TWEEN_TIME`, after which the part is destroyed and\\nthe entry cleared. Otherwise `onClaim` is spawned and the drop goes\\nstraight to [DropsController.removeDrop]. Both paths play `item-pickup`.\\n\\n:::caution\\nErrors on an unknown `dropId` \u2014 it indexes `activeDrops` without a guard.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"dropId","desc":"Key into the active-drops table","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"forcePickup","desc":"Bypass the radius, delay and arrival checks","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1032,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"checkClaims","desc":"Claim sweep. Driven every RenderStepped by the connection\\n[DropsController.start] opens.\\n\\nBails early when there is no character pivot, otherwise offers every\\nactive drop to [DropsController.pickupDrop], which applies the radius and\\ndelay checks per drop.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1176,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"start","desc":"Bootstrap hook, run after [DropsController.init]. Opens the RenderStepped\\nconnection that drives [DropsController.checkClaims].","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1197,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"shutdown","desc":"Tears the controller down: disconnects the claim and update loops and\\ncalls [DropsController.clearAllDrops]. Idempotent \u2014 both connections are\\nnil-checked and nil\'d out, so [DropsController.init] and\\n[DropsController.start] can bring it back up.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1216,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"DropData","desc":"Everything a caller can ask for when spawning a drop. Only `particle` is\\nrequired.\\n\\nIf `tweenTarget` is omitted, the origin doubles as the target and\\n`targetSpread` is forced on, so a drop always travels *somewhere* rather\\nthan landing on itself. Both spread flags apply a random offset of up to\\n`DROP_SPREAD_RADIUS` studs horizontally and 0..2 vertically.","fields":[{"name":"origin","lua_type":"Vector3?","desc":"Spawn point. Defaults to the character\'s PrimaryPart position"},{"name":"originSpread","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Randomize the spawn point"},{"name":"tweenTarget","lua_type":"Vector3?","desc":"Landing point before the ground raycast. Defaults to `origin`"},{"name":"targetSpread","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Randomize the landing point. Forced true when `tweenTarget` is nil"},{"name":"particle","lua_type":"BasePart | string","desc":"Part to clone, or an image asset id rendered as a billboard"},{"name":"lifetime","lua_type":"number?","desc":"Seconds before expiry. Defaults to `DROP_LIFETIME`"},{"name":"onClaim","lua_type":"(() -> ())?","desc":"Fired on claim, and on cleanup when the drop was never claimed"},{"name":"tweenToCharacterOnClaim","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Fly to the character on claim instead of vanishing"},{"name":"destroyOnArrival","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Skip the idle float; retire as soon as the arc lands"},{"name":"autoClaimOnDestruction","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"On expiry, force a pickup instead of a silent removal"}],"source":{"line":157,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"Drop","desc":"The resolved form of a [DropData], returned by\\n[DropsController.spawnDrop]. `claimed` and `tweenInProgress` are the two\\nguards that keep the animation systems from fighting: once `claimed` is\\nset, the idle float disconnects itself and nothing else may move the part.","fields":[{"name":"particle","lua_type":"BasePart","desc":"The live instance in Workspace"},{"name":"targetPosition","lua_type":"Vector3","desc":"Ground position the arc lands on; claim distance is measured to this"},{"name":"lifetime","lua_type":"number","desc":"Resolved seconds before expiry"},{"name":"createdAt","lua_type":"number","desc":"`os.clock()` at spawn"},{"name":"onClaim","lua_type":"(() -> ())?","desc":"Caller\'s claim callback"},{"name":"tweenToCharacterOnClaim","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Fly to the character on claim"},{"name":"autoClaimOnDestruction","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Force a pickup on expiry"},{"name":"claimed","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Set once claimed; freezes all position updates"},{"name":"tweenInProgress","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"A pickup lerp is running"},{"name":"destroyOnArrival","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Retire on landing instead of floating"}],"source":{"line":190,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}},{"name":"DropInfo","desc":"Internal bookkeeping entry, one per live drop, keyed by drop id in the\\nmodule-local `activeDrops` table. The maid owns every connection and tween\\nthe drop created; destroying it stops all of them at once.","fields":[{"name":"maid","lua_type":"Maid.Maid","desc":"Owns the drop\'s connections, tweens and particle"},{"name":"dropData","lua_type":"Drop","desc":"The drop itself"},{"name":"createdAt","lua_type":"number","desc":"`os.clock()` at spawn; expiry and `CLAIM_DELAY` are measured from here"},{"name":"destroying","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Set while retiring, so the update/claim loops skip it"}],"private":true,"source":{"line":217,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}}],"name":"DropsController","desc":"Purely-cosmetic loot drops: the coin/item that arcs out of a mined node,\\nfloats on the ground, and flies into your character when you walk up to it.\\n\\nNothing here is authoritative. The server has already granted the reward\\nbefore a drop is spawned; this controller animates it and fires the\\ncaller\'s `onClaim` callback at the right moment. A player who never walks\\nover a drop still gets the reward if the caller asked for\\n`autoClaimOnDestruction`.\\n\\n### Lifecycle\\n\\n1. **Spawn** \u2014 [DropsController.spawnDrop] clones or builds the particle\\n   part, resolves an origin (caller\'s `origin`, else the character\'s\\n   PrimaryPart) and a landing target, then raycasts `RAYCAST_DISTANCE`\\n   studs straight down from the target to find ground. Assets under\\n   `ReplicatedStorage.Assets.DropsAssets` are cloned onto the part; if one\\n   of them is a `RewardTrail`, two attachments are created for it. Plays\\n   the `item-drop` SFX.\\n2. **Flight** \u2014 a 3-point [Bezier] (start, a control point `DROP_ARC_HEIGHT`\\n   studs above the midpoint scaled by distance, landing spot) drives a\\n   CFrame tween over `DROP_FLIGHT_DURATION`. A parallel RenderStepped\\n   connection adds tumbling spin. On completion the trail is disabled and\\n   the part snaps to the landing CFrame.\\n3. **Idle** \u2014 unless `destroyOnArrival` ended it at step 2, the part starts\\n   a sine float: vertical offset of `ITEM_FLOAT_DISTANCE` on a\\n   `FLOATING_PERIOD`-second period, a half-rate horizontal wobble, and a\\n   slow continuous yaw. Runs on RenderStepped and self-disconnects if the\\n   part is deparented or gets claimed.\\n4. **Claim** \u2014 [DropsController.checkClaims] runs every RenderStepped and\\n   offers every active drop to [DropsController.pickupDrop]. A drop is\\n   claimable once it is within `DEFAULT_CLAIM_RADIUS` studs of the\\n   character *and* at least `CLAIM_DELAY` seconds old \u2014 the delay is what\\n   stops a drop spawned at your feet from vanishing before you see it.\\n5. **Pickup** \u2014 with `tweenToCharacterOnClaim`, the trail is re-enabled and\\n   a RenderStepped lerp pulls the part to the character\'s *current* pivot\\n   over `CHARACTER_TWEEN_TIME`, re-reading the pivot each frame so it\\n   tracks a moving player. Otherwise `onClaim` fires and the drop is\\n   removed immediately. Either path plays the `item-pickup` SFX.\\n6. **Expiry** \u2014 [DropsController.updateDrops] runs every RenderStepped and\\n   retires anything older than its `lifetime` (default `DROP_LIFETIME`),\\n   force-claiming it first when `autoClaimOnDestruction` is set.\\n\\n### Timing constants\\n\\nThese are load-bearing and interact:\\n\\n| Constant | Default | What depends on it |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `DROP_FLIGHT_DURATION` | 0.3 | Bezier tween length *and* the tumble connection\'s own alpha clock \u2014 they must match or the spin cuts out early |\\n| `CLAIM_DELAY` | 0.2 | Measured from `dropInfo.createdAt`, i.e. from spawn, not from landing. Keep it under `DROP_FLIGHT_DURATION` and drops become claimable mid-flight |\\n| `CHARACTER_TWEEN_TIME` | 0.2 | Pickup lerp. The particle is destroyed when it elapses, so raising it leaves the part visible longer after the SFX |\\n| `DROP_LIFETIME` | 20 | Default expiry, overridable per drop |\\n| `FLOATING_PERIOD` | 2 | Idle sine period |\\n| `DEFAULT_CLAIM_RADIUS` | 10 | Claim distance, measured against the drop\'s *target* position, not its animated position |\\n| `PARTICLE_TEXT_LIFE` | 3 | [DropsController.showChange] popup lifetime and its tween duration |\\n\\n### Floating numbers\\n\\n[DropsController.showChange] is a separate system that happens to live\\nhere. It welds one billboard to the character and accumulates gains into\\nit: repeated calls within `PARTICLE_TEXT_LIFE` seconds bump the running\\ntotal and reset the timer rather than spawning a second popup, and each\\ndistinct `{unitType}_{itemId}` gets its own label row inside the shared\\nbillboard.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":73,"path":"src/Client/Features/Core/Controllers/DropsController.luau"}}')}}]);